<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The Lindwyrm ~ Referee Dossier

''The public meme tells the truth and stops early.'' This dossier carries the working layer
beneath: what she runs, through whom, and toward what. The deepest strata — her history with
Telarus, the sealed lore of the Breakings' true shape — ''ride the operator's own memory seats
and never draft here''; this meme points at their existence and carries none of their content.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-apparatus>>

!! The Apparatus

* ''Rhea the Moon Elf'' — her intelligence-mistress; a trained cadre and a small network whose
  Neo-Thracian intel of the last two months set the summit's timing. Wash-outs from Rhea's cut
  flow to the Adventurer's Guild, which keeps the partner company stocked with vetted talent.
  ([[dossier|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/npcs/rhea-the-moon-elf]])
* ''Captain Melantha Vex'' — the respectable cut-out: Guild-Captain paperwork over selective
  disclosure; standing instructions to deliver Lady Aki to the Ainos corridor and recover any
  pre-Breaking pilotage scrap en route. ([[dossier|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/characters/npcs/melantha-vex]])
* ''The Adventurer's Guild'' — the partner company and the deniable hand: contracts where a
  Patroness's direct hand would tilt the politics.
* ''The House of Masks'' — the Order of Amaranth's floor, her preferred neutral ground; the
  whispered liminal ways beneath it reach where a dragon prefers not to be seen traveling.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-long-game>>

!! The Long Game

''The summit runs as a recruitment engine.'' The broadcast's paid-holiday generosity reads as
bait, and everyone signing knows it — which keeps it honest. The real agenda sits at the empty
seat: ''Neo-Thracia'', thirteen months past the storm's breaking, the Hebros mouth navigable
four months running, the Dominion mapping another league of coast each season the window
narrows. The Credit Compact's generous terms buy her the one thing a hoard cannot: ''companies
willing to walk into a broken Nexus and relight it one herm at a time.''

''What she watches:'' the Dominion's scout legion on the coastal road · Krull's Amaranth company
in the passes · the Courts' agents she pretends not to track and tracks · the window.

''What she protects:'' the mesh itself. The DreamNet stands on her hoard's orichalcum; every
relit lararium extends the thing she spent centuries preparing without admitting she was
preparing it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/form-and-seals>>

!! Form, and the Sealed Strata

''Her body — blessed canon (2026-08-15), referee-side:'' the heraldic lindworm law holds true —
''wingless, serpentine, two forelimbs only'', scales in orichalcum-sheen, her hoard's metal
grown into her body. ''Register (Freyja's canon):'' very eastern — Miyazaki / Earthsea /
Spirited-Away dragon-language — crossed with the German wingless line; ''Master-tier heritage
with levitation-flight'' (she flies the way rivers swim, no wings asked). The insulation from
the Great Game read as strategy in hindsight and as temperament in truth: the conclave of 5002
convened at her table because hers was the only neutral one, and neutrality that old converts
to authority overnight. ''The table itself (operator-felt, Provisional):'' a hidden
astral-dream-realm hoard-room, connected to what became the House of Masks — her vault cleared
for company; the low door that breathes may open on it still, which reads the RSVP card's "I
will use the door" at its full depth. ''She never flew; she levitated a city instead'' — a wingless dragon who
solved flight by engineering, which explains more of her career than any prophecy. Her humanoid
dragon-kin form rides as ''a kept shed skin, worn like couture'' (the folktale seam: the
lindworm transforms by shedding); the mana-muting glamour reads as "the last shift." The public
meme's witnesses-disagree line stays TRUE and stays published — she corrects no one, and the
disagreement serves her.

''Sealed strata, pointed at, never carried:'' her finding of Telarus and the debt between them ·
the true shape of what broke at the Second Breaking and what she knows of it · the reasons a
dragon builds meshes. These live referee-side of even this bag — the operator's seats alone.

